     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><u></u> <u></u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:10pt\">Hi... I&#39;m new on the secr\r\nmodels and I want to know your advice on what is the best approuch to define on/\r\nof road as a covariate at detectors station.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\">\r\n<br><br>\r\n<span style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">And how is the best way to write a model to put on model\r\nselection under AIC  in  where the placement of the detectors (on/of\r\nroad) can have an effect on capture probabilities?</span><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<span style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Is that  some mixed models writing with </span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial,sans-serif;border-width:1pt;border-style:none;border-color:windowtext;padding:0cm;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"> d~cover,\r\nbk</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"> or BK (site specifics response) ? </span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif\"><br>\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<span style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Thank you very much</span></span><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt;line-height:115%;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><u></u><u></u></span></p></div>"
    ]
