   "subject": "Re: Best way to add categorical spatial covariates of detector station (on/off road)",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You should be able to get this by reading the documentation (recommended), but...<br>Define a 2-level &#39;traps&#39; covariate and use its name in the model. If you already have a capthist object CH and vector x of codes, one per detector, then the covariate dataframe can be added and used with<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">covariates</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">traps</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">onoff </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><code><span style=\"color:#000\">fit0 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g0 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> 1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> etc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#000\"></span></code><code><span style=\"color:#000\">fitroad </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g0 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> onoff</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> etc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#000\">AIC(fit0, fitroad)<br>predict(fitroad, newdata = data.frame(onoff = levels(factor(x))))<br></span></code><span style=\"color:#000\"></span></div></code></div>Murray</div>"
    ],
